                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 7,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I am in Macon and Warner Robins today to talk about how the Big Ugly Bill gutted affordable healthcare for Georgians and the ongoing attacks on federal workers who are vital to our communities \u2013 from the VA and our military installations to our city and county offices helping support housing, agriculture, food safety, and more!\n\nTake it from the doctors and patient advocates who serve our community. They are letting us know what is at risk if Congress fails to prevent the imminent skyrocketing of healthcare premiums. People\u2019s lives are at risk. Our hospitals and nursing homes are at risk.\n\nThat is why I am continuing to fight for Georgians and help protect affordable healthcare for millions of Americans.\n\nhttps://t.co/T21YvdpKXr",
